  "summary": "Fixes edge cases and potential assertion crashes in `CheckBlockDataAvailability`. The availability check previously checked whether the upper block had any requested bit rather than all of them, which could trigger an assertion inside `GetFirstBlock`. The change also corrects handling around genesis undo data, which could improperly reject undo-only requests, accept missing block data, or misjudge ranges containing only genesis.",
  "problem": "In block storage availability checks, callers requesting multiple data flags could hit an assertion in `GetFirstBlock` if the upper block only satisfied a subset of the requested mask. Additionally, logic accounting for genesis having no undo data had multiple flaws: it could accept blocks missing block data if another bit matched, reject valid undo-only requests spanning down to genesis, and mishandle single-block genesis ranges.",
